{
  "id": "media.reduced-mtu-full-size",
  "category": "media-plane",
  "spec_cite": [
    "docs/wire-protocol-v2/spec.md §7.3 (payload_max = max_datagram_size() − 24, re-queried at send time, D2)",
    "docs/wire-protocol-v2/spec.md §11.2 (path MTU 1280 profile)",
    "docs/wire-protocol-v2/spec.md §2 D2 (prototype: mds 1192 at path MTU 1280)"
  ],
  "description": "Reduced path MTU (DPLPMTUD converged at mds = 1192, the value the prototype observed at path MTU 1280): payload_max = 1168 = 146 whole F32LE stereo frames — the datagram is sized to the CURRENT limit at send time.",
  "preconditions": [
    "Session PLAYING; instance 5, generation 1; 48 kHz stereo F32LE.",
    "The limit is this session's CURRENT max_datagram_size() (1192) — never a fixed 1464/1500 assumption, never cached across path changes (D2)."
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "kind": "datagram",
      "index": 1,
      "dir": "S->C",
      "channel": "datagram",
      "datagram_hex": "",
      "length": 1192,
      "decoded": {
        "stream_instance_id": 5,
        "config_generation": 1,
        "sequence": 0,
        "timestamp": 0,
        "flags": "0x00000001",
        "flags_set": [
          "STREAM_START"
        ],
        "payload_bytes": 1168,
        "payload_frames": 146,
        "frame_bytes": 8
      },
      "note": "payload_max = 1192 − 24 = 1168; 146 frames; STREAM_START."
    }
  ],
  "assertions": [
    "payload_max = max_datagram_size() − 24, re-queried per send (D2); receivers MUST NOT validate a sender's datagram size against their own local limit (D2).",
    "Frame alignment holds exactly at the limit here: 1168 % 8 == 0. For a limit that does not divide evenly see media/reduced-mtu-alignment-floor.",
    "Payload bytes are the synthetic ramp; alignment and sizing are what the vector pins.",
    "If the path limit drops further, the next datagram is simply smaller (per-send sizing); oversized sends fail and are re-chunked or dropped (§7.3)."
  ]
}
